MID_EV14_054_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_054_m01_001: Leda, there you are! I beg of you—can we speak?
MID_EV14_054_m01_002: I have nothing to say to you.
MID_EV14_054_m01_003: Then just listen. Please, if only for a moment.
MID_EV14_054_m01_004: There's a chasm between the two of us. What on\nearth could you say that I would care about?
MID_EV14_054_m01_005: You were raised in a palace. You're the queen of\nArago now!
MID_EV14_054_m01_006: What did you ever want for?!
MID_EV14_054_m01_007: I suppose...the freedom to make my own choices.
MID_EV14_054_m01_008: I was bound by duty to make myself worthy of\nthe throne—and in time, inherit it.
MID_EV14_054_m01_009: I was trained in combat and the arts and kingcraft\nfrom childhood. Hardly ever given a break.
MID_EV14_054_m01_010: My only respite was the time I got to spend with my\ncherished friends.
MID_EV14_054_m01_011: One of whom, I take it, was Bertrand.
MID_EV14_054_m01_012: Yes. And Gilchris, the man I would go on to marry.\nI treasure the memories of our time together.
MID_EV14_054_m01_013: Men are all the same. No sooner do you look\nthe other way than they get up to something.
MID_EV14_054_m01_014: These friends of yours might have done some\nheinous things while you weren't paying attention.
MID_EV14_054_m01_015: Making countless people you don't even know\nresent you.
MID_EV14_054_m01_016: Everyone in a royal family is resented to\nsome extent.
MID_EV14_054_m01_017: But as the daughter of Aragonian royalty, I am\nbraced for it.
MID_EV14_054_m01_018: You can't make any decision as a monarch without\nalso making an enemy.
MID_EV14_054_m01_019: After all, there are armies under your control,\ncarrying out their duties by your orders.
MID_EV14_054_m01_020: And the mistakes they make become the monarch's\nresponsibility.
MID_EV14_054_m01_021: I've met a fair number of soldiers in my time, and to\nsay they make "mistakes" is an understatement.
MID_EV14_054_m01_022: They're a bunch of bastards, interested only in\nlining their pockets.
MID_EV14_054_m01_023: If I were queen I'd be a little more reluctant to take\nresponsibility for jackals like that.
MID_EV14_054_m01_024: Well... There's a mistake I made too. One I can't\nforgive myself for.
MID_EV14_054_m01_025: And what's that? Marrying someone else when you\nwere in love with Bertrand?
MID_EV14_054_m01_026: No... Allowing my faith in Bertrand to falter.
MID_EV14_054_m01_027: That's why I have to help him however I can.
MID_EV14_054_m01_028: {SetColor=Gray}What is she going to think of me...after I kill him?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV14_054_m01_029: It doesn't matter. You said you had something you\nwanted to talk about.
MID_EV14_054_m01_030: Indeed. An invitation.
MID_EV14_054_m01_031: We'll be hosting a banquet at the guesthouse where\nwe're staying.
MID_EV14_054_m01_032: Would you consider honoring the event with one of\nyour masterful performances?
MID_EV14_054_m01_033: A banquet, you said? Hm...
MID_EV14_054_m01_034: And you agreed? This could very well be a trap.
MID_EV14_054_m01_035: If the kingdom of Arago is connected to this\nconspiracy, I see the logic in attending.
MID_EV14_054_m01_036: Whether it's a trap or not, going into enemy territory\nmight be our only way to learn more.
MID_EV14_054_m01_037: Well! It's a banquet. Banquets have lots of people.\nEspecially this one, probably, if it's a big Arago thing!
MID_EV14_054_m01_038: I bet it won't be too hard to blend in.
MID_EV14_054_m01_039: I will come with you, of course!
MID_EV14_054_m01_040: There is no tableau in which I sparkle more vividly\nthan a good banquet.
MID_EV14_054_m01_041: Besides, Leilidahna! You chose to trust Queen\nAswan, did you not?
MID_EV14_054_m01_042: Well...she keeps making it seem like she wants to be\nmy friend.
MID_EV14_054_m01_043: I thought I'd trust her this once.
MID_EV14_055_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_055_m01_001: *sigh*
MID_EV14_055_m01_002: You stopped. I'm not interrupting, am I?
MID_EV14_055_m01_003: It's fine, Sister. Something to say?
MID_EV14_055_m01_004: No, no—just listening. Beauuutiful melody. I could\nreally feel you putting your heart in it.
MID_EV14_055_m01_005: Probably a song about... Heehee. About love, right?
MID_EV14_055_m01_006: It's just a song. One I wrote for someone long ago.\nI suppose I'm feeling nostalgic.
MID_EV14_055_m01_007: So, it's true! You were in looove. Mahna got\nbit bad, huh?
MID_EV14_055_m01_008: You parted ways a long time ago and your heart just\ncan't stop yearning for someone.
MID_EV14_055_m01_009: Someone who's not Father. A human, I bet!
MID_EV14_055_m01_010: None of this is your concern.
MID_EV14_055_m01_011: Eeheehee! It's too good!
MID_EV14_055_m01_012: What did it feel like? Watching the human you\nloved, and the child you painfully pushed out...
MID_EV14_055_m01_013: Watching them die so long before you. I'm curious.\nReally, I am.
MID_EV14_055_m01_014: Enough.
MID_EV14_055_m01_015: See, I've never loved anyone other than Father.
MID_EV14_055_m01_016: Hehe. Yu Phas—our big sister. She fell in love with\nSolel and it ruined her!
MID_EV14_055_m01_017: Nothing good comes from falling for anyone\nbut Father.
MID_EV14_055_m01_018: You're a grown-up, Mahna. How is it you forgot to\nuse your head?
MID_EV14_055_m01_019: It's OK, though. You'll see this person again when\nwe manifest the underworld.
MID_EV14_055_m01_020: Why do you think I'm doing this?
MID_EV14_055_m01_021: But...who knows if they'll still be them! They may\nnot have their old heart!
MID_EV14_055_m01_022: Hahaha... AHAHAHA!
MID_EV14_055_m01_023: Grrr...
MID_EV14_055_m01_024: Eishet, stop talking. From all I've heard, you are\nbeing exceptionally childish.
MID_EV14_055_m01_025: Well, Lyrah! You must have missed the part where\nshe was being hilarious.
MID_EV14_055_m01_026: Mahna's in love with a human!
MID_EV14_055_m01_027: I mean, it's so stupid. She's so stupid! I love it.
MID_EV14_055_m01_028: I thought I told you to stop talking.
MID_EV14_055_m01_029: Hmph!
MID_EV14_055_m01_030: Thank you, Sister. Another minute more and I would\nhave killed her.
MID_EV14_055_m01_031: Which is exactly why I stepped in.
MID_EV14_055_m01_032: The truth is that Eishet is right on the mark.\nCohen is the man I loved.
MID_EV14_055_m01_033: I want to manifest the underworld so that I can\nresurrect him.
MID_EV14_055_m01_034: On the subject of the bard... I got a concerning report\nfrom someone watching his descendant.
MID_EV14_055_m01_035: Queen Aswan invited Leda to the banquet? Hmm.\nNot the worst outcome at all.
MID_EV14_055_m01_036: The girl's been interfering so much lately. Perhaps it's\ntime we deal with the Rose of Caelus.
MID_EV14_055_m01_037: Pluck some petals. She lives, she lives not...
MID_EV14_056_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_056_m01_001: Leda, you're so pretty! You look like a princess.
MID_EV14_056_m01_002: That's kind. But it's been years since I wore\nsomething like this. How out of place will I look?
MID_EV14_056_m01_003: Not at all. I can't help but feel wistful, milady.
MID_EV14_056_m01_004: If only Lord Guillermo were here to see you.
MID_EV14_056_m01_005: Your beauty has never been in question, but in\nthis outfit, you're positively glamorous.
MID_EV14_056_m01_006: Yes, Leilidahna! Exactly what I'd expect from my\nworthiest rival.
MID_EV14_056_m01_007: All eyes at the banquet will be on us!
MID_EV14_056_m01_008: That is not our goal. In fact, I'd prefer that we\ndidn't stand out.
MID_EV14_056_m01_009: So, Olympia, are you used to...whatever it is that\nhappens at banquets?
MID_EV14_056_m01_010: Indeed. But it's been a while since I was at a\nsocial gathering like this.
MID_EV14_056_m01_011: I stopped attending them after I began serving at\nKalla's temple.
MID_EV14_056_m01_012: But the key, Mu, is not to worry! Or...not to show\nyour worry. Keep your head held high.
MID_EV14_056_m01_013: Hehe... I'll try. I've never worn anything\nthis...expensive?
MID_EV14_056_m01_014: <NCA>Compliment her.
MID_EV14_056_m01_015: It suits you, Mu. You look good in girls' clothes too.
MID_EV14_056_m01_016: Thanks, Leda! I'm glad to hear you say that.
MID_EV14_056_m01_017: Chancellor Martila, your visitors are here.
MID_EV14_056_m01_018: Hmhmhm. Arrived on time! Well then. The plan\nclicks into place.
MID_EV14_056_m01_019: Send them to the other room, please.
MID_EV14_056_m01_020: Yes, ma'am.
MID_EV14_056_m01_021: What could have happened? The banquet's\nstarting soon, and no sign of Leda.
MID_EV14_056_m01_022: The woman you told me about. She's not here?
MID_EV14_056_m01_023: That's right—my dear friend who came to my aid\nin the city.
MID_EV14_056_m01_024: She can be intimidating to speak to, and by\nappearances, quite busy.
MID_EV14_056_m01_025: But I would have liked to see her today. Ask her\nsome questions about herself.
MID_EV14_056_m01_026: You don't think... Could something be wrong?\nShe said she'd make it.
MID_EV14_056_m01_027: No one passes through. No one.
MID_EV14_056_m01_028: And now...we begin.
MID_EV14_056_m01_029: With flamma and the power of Moonstone, I can\nbriefly manifest the underworld here.
MID_EV14_056_m01_030: Even with my abilities...it will not be easy.
MID_EV14_056_m01_031: But the Rose of Caelus's arrival merits\nsome hospitality.
MID_EV14_057_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_057_m01_001: Your patience is appreciated. This way, please.
MID_EV14_057_m01_002: Ah! Rather different from what I expected. It's so...\nHow do I put this politely? Bleak.
MID_EV14_057_m01_003: Milady, I don't think these are guests at a party.\nThey may be serving our enemy.
MID_EV14_057_m01_004: <NCA>Look around.
MID_EV14_057_m01_005: Aswan seemed so sincere about being my friend.
MID_EV14_057_m01_006: I'm sick and tired of getting stabbed in the back.
MID_EV14_057_m01_007: Leilidahna? You're here too?
MID_EV14_057_m01_008: Mandalan? But how— How do you know that name?
MID_EV14_057_m01_009: Rose of Caelus! You accepted my invitation. Oh, I'm\nso thrilled.
MID_EV14_057_m01_010: As thanks, I'll even disclose a secret or two.
MID_EV14_057_m01_011: What are you talking about? The Cydonia Massacre?
MID_EV14_057_m01_012: It was merely a farce put on to dig up orichalcum\nfrom the land there.
MID_EV14_057_m01_013: Which we did, after a considerable effort to deceive\nthe Divine Sovereign.
MID_EV14_057_m01_014: And why exactly was it that you needed such a large\nquantity of orichalcum?
MID_EV14_057_m01_015: To fix something. Something out of the ordinary.
MID_EV14_057_m01_016: The needed amount's been acquired, despite your\nunanticipated meddling...
MID_EV14_057_m01_017: And our subordinates expecting more, and more,\nand more!
MID_EV14_057_m01_018: I mean, really—after all the wealth they'd amassed!\nHumans. You're so greedy!
MID_EV14_057_m01_019: Anyway, we had to get rid of them. So we did.\nWell...you did.
MID_EV14_057_m01_020: That little list from our friend Mahdel.
MID_EV14_057_m01_021: Are you saying... There was a connection between\nyou and Father Mahdel?
MID_EV14_057_m01_022: Give a curtsy, dear! You danced beautifully for us.
MID_EV14_057_m01_023: The Rose of Caelus took out the hindrances to our\nplan one by one—as we'd hoped.
MID_EV14_057_m01_024: Mandalan, while we're sharing secrets, perhaps it's\ntime to finally show your face.
MID_EV14_057_m01_025: Rrrghhh...
MID_EV14_057_m01_026: Father Mahdel, no! How? You... You framed Father!
MID_EV14_057_m01_027: In my time at Dagsion, I researched endlessly ways\nof bringing the dead back to life.
MID_EV14_057_m01_028: I was a high priest here. And my best friend,\nGuillermo—I wanted so badly to exceed him.
MID_EV14_057_m01_029: Then I found I'd been infected with an incurable\ndisease...
MID_EV14_057_m01_030: and my research changed in focus, and it became\nmore passionate. More urgent.
MID_EV14_057_m01_031: I tried everything. I kept failing and failing. Then in\nthe deepest depths of my despair, they came.
MID_EV14_057_m01_032: The Order of Mithras.
MID_EV14_057_m01_033: The Order gave me the answer I'd been so long\nunable to find.
MID_EV14_057_m01_034: One of Drake's treasures. Within it lay the power to\nslow the progression of my disease.
MID_EV14_057_m01_035: Yet over time, my anger at Guillermo did not\ndie down. It grew.
MID_EV14_057_m01_036: So when the Order of Mithras approached me with a\nplan to take Cydonia...
MID_EV14_057_m01_037: I agreed at once. I saw it as the perfect chance to\ntake my revenge on Guillermo.
MID_EV14_057_m01_038: Drake's treasures eat away at their owner's spirit.\nYours amplified your negative emotions.
MID_EV14_057_m01_039: It made you a pliable servant for the Order\nof Mithras.
MID_EV14_057_m01_040: After the Siege of Cydonia, I began living a double\nlife as both Mahdel and Mandalan.
MID_EV14_057_m01_041: My interests in Cydonia made me—as Mandalan—\na very successful merchant.
MID_EV14_057_m01_042: It was time to bid my old identity farewell, so I set\nfire to the shrine as cover for my disappearance.
MID_EV14_057_m01_043: But...the blaze was more extreme than I'd planned.\nI emerged nearly dead, with burns all over my body.
MID_EV14_057_m01_044: I trusted you, Father Mahdel. I trusted you!
MID_EV14_057_m01_045: Leda? Something really weird just happened!
MID_EV14_057_m01_046: Impossible! This can't be the land of the living.\nWe're in the underworld.
MID_EV14_057_m01_047: Yes. Soon to be your permanent residence.
MID_EV14_058_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_058_m01_001: I did not think you capable of turning your weapon\nagainst your father... It seems I misjudged.
MID_EV14_058_m01_002: Well, no matter. You will not be able to escape\nthe underworld.
MID_EV14_058_m01_003: You'll be trapped here, which means you're as good\nas dead!
MID_EV14_058_m01_004: Father... I've caused you even more suffering...
MID_EV14_058_m01_005: Leilidahna... I...
MID_EV14_058_m01_006: This guy's still breathing, Leda!
MID_EV14_058_m01_007: Why did you hate Father so much? He considered\nyou his best friend.
MID_EV14_058_m01_008: I had been in love with Hilaria. Your poor mother,\nborn with such frailty.
MID_EV14_058_m01_009: But she chose Guillermo. And she gave birth to you.\nThen departed this life so young...
MID_EV14_058_m01_010: I had to bring her back to me, so I began studying\nways of returning the dead to life.
MID_EV14_058_m01_011: Never did I forgive Guillermo for taking Hilaria away\nfrom me. For letting her die!
MID_EV14_058_m01_012: What?! But neither Father nor Mother meant to...
MID_EV14_058_m01_013: I know. I knew it even then. But if I let go of my\nhatred of him...
MID_EV14_058_m01_014: I did love you like you were my own daughter.\nThat... That was never a lie.
MID_EV14_058_m01_015: Leilidahna. Please forgive me...
MID_EV14_058_m01_016: *cough* Urgh...
MID_EV14_058_m01_017: Father Mahdel.
MID_EV14_058_m01_018: Miss Leda, I apologize, but our circumstances\nare grim. We have no time to waste.
MID_EV14_058_m01_019: If we don't make our escape immediately, we may\nbe trapped forever.
MID_EV14_058_m01_020: Leilidahna! How long are you planning to wallow\nin your misery?
MID_EV14_058_m01_021: You're hardly going to defeat Bertrand if you're stuck\nin here!
MID_EV14_058_m01_022: I mean, really! You thought yourself worthy to be\nmy rival? A coward like you?
MID_EV14_058_m01_023: <NCA>Stand up.
MID_EV14_058_m01_024: Thanks, Olympia. You're right... I still have that.
MID_EV14_058_m01_025: Bertrand is still alive, and I'm going to kill him.
MID_EV14_058_m01_026: Yes! There is the Leilidahna I know.
MID_EV14_058_m01_027: I'm glad milady is back on her feet but...it's not clear\nwhere we can go.
MID_EV14_058_m01_028: Well, we certainly cannot just stand around here.\nLet's move, swift as a hurricane!
MID_EV14_058_m01_029: Goodbye, Father Mahdel.
MID_EV14_058_m01_030: Another fork! Uh...which way do we go?
MID_EV14_058_m01_031: Hard to say...and if we choose incorrectly, it may be\nthe end for us.
MID_EV14_058_m01_032: Miss Leda...will you choose?
MID_EV14_058_m01_033: What? How the hell am I supposed to know?!
MID_EV14_058_m01_034: You don't! None of us do. So it might as well be you\nthat chooses.
MID_EV14_058_m01_035: Haaah... Haaah...
MID_EV14_058_m01_036: Why all this hemming and hawing?! The exit's\nthat way!
MID_EV14_058_m01_037: Who the HECK is that? And how did they get here?!
MID_EV14_058_m01_038: It's...you! You're the one I saw all that time ago.
MID_EV14_058_m01_039: I knew 'twould be easier to see you here, close\nas it is to the world of the dead.
MID_EV14_058_m01_040: But the spell is broken, and this place is beginning to\ncollapse. Time is of the essence.
MID_EV14_058_m01_041: So fly hence with all your speed!
MID_EV14_058_m01_042: I'm grateful to you... Whoever you are.\nWe'll make way.
MID_EV14_059_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_059_m01_001: Ah... Is this...the guesthouse?
MID_EV14_059_m01_002: I suppose that means we made it out safely.
MID_EV14_059_m01_003: Where did you all come from?
MID_EV14_059_m01_004: I see, so this is the banquet hall. Well...we're hardly\nin any shape for a banquet.
MID_EV14_059_m01_005: Leda! There you are!
MID_EV14_059_m01_006: I've been so looking forward to this. How long ago did\nyou get here? I wish you would have let me know...
MID_EV14_059_m01_007: Ah?! Leda?
MID_EV14_059_m01_008: Do NOT touch me!
MID_EV14_059_m01_009: What in heaven's name is wrong?
MID_EV14_059_m01_010: Talk to me, please. I don't know what I did to\nupset you...
MID_EV14_059_m01_011: Listen to me, Aswan. I WILL kill Bertrand.
MID_EV14_059_m01_012: If anyone gets in my way, I will show them\nno mercy. And that includes you.
MID_EV14_059_m01_013: What are you talking about? Why are you so intent\non killing Bertrand?
MID_EV14_059_m01_014: *sob* Father... My father...
MID_EV14_059_m01_015: Milady...
MID_EV14_059_m01_016: There's nothing we can do for her right now, Buccar.
MID_EV14_059_m01_017: I think we'd better leave her be.
MID_EV14_059_m01_018: Maybe you're right.
MID_EV14_059_m01_019: Is Leda going to be OK?
MID_EV14_059_m01_020: I have no doubt. She is my worthy rival, after all.
MID_EV14_059_m01_021: I wonder what it was that Father Mahdel\nultimately wanted.
MID_EV14_059_m01_022: He did say he loved Lady Leda as if she were his\nown daughter.
MID_EV14_059_m01_023: Perhaps he saw a resemblance of her late mother,\nLady Hilaria.
MID_EV14_059_m01_024: On the other hand, he had mixed feelings about\nLord Guillermo, which the Order exploited.
MID_EV14_059_m01_025: He risked everything to fake his own death and\ndisappear...
MID_EV14_059_m01_026: Perhaps he did that to hide the truth of his crimes\nfrom Lady Leda.
MID_EV14_059_m01_027: Ahhh... That would...certainly explain his actions.
MID_EV14_059_m01_028: Chancellor Martila! You're hurt. We must treat you\nat once.
MID_EV14_059_m01_029: I'm fine. Leave me alone.
MID_EV14_059_m01_030: I thought it was impossible for the Rose of Caelus\nto escape...
MID_EV14_059_m01_031: How did this happen? Who's protecting her?
MID_EV14_059_m01_032: Either way, I miscalculated. I'll need to tell\nmy sister...